B.bY6=new A.a(B.a,["Wrestling | Spine | Hip Flexor Strain | Return To Sport | Advanced | Lesson 5000","Definition\\n- This lesson explains how Spine mechanics, Rotation patterning, and Return To Sport apply to Wrestling with emphasis on Hip Flexor Strain management.\\n\\nWhy it matters\\n- Better movement decisions improve tissue tolerance, control load, and support safer performance progression.\\n\\nHow to apply it\\n- Assess baseline quality, choose the smallest effective change, monitor symptoms, and progress only when quality remains stable.\\n\\nCommon mistakes\\n- Progressing too fast, ignoring fatigue, using one intervention for every athlete, and skipping movement quality checks.\\n\\nQuick self-check\\n- Can you identify the main limitation, the best regression, the best progression, and the key coaching cue for this case?",u.uF,"Advanced",B.ajN,"Hip Flexor Strain","Wrestling","Spine","Return To Sport","Advanced","Rotation","rehabilitation",5000],t.R)
